1066
00:50:02.090 --> 00:50:02.710
Did you hear that?
你们听到了吗？

1067
00:50:03.390 --> 00:50:05.390
I got into a big debate with my family.
我和家人为此争论了很久。

1068
00:50:05.390 --> 00:50:07.930
They were positive that he was saying Albert.
他们坚信他说的是阿尔伯特。

1069
00:50:07.970 --> 00:50:09.270
And I said, no, it's Elbert.
我说不，是埃尔伯特。

1070
00:50:09.450 --> 00:50:11.150
I know I'm hearing Elbert.
我知道我听到的是埃尔伯特。

1071
00:50:11.430 --> 00:50:14.710
It's weird because her father's name is Elbert.
真奇怪，因为她父亲的名字就叫埃尔伯特。

1072
00:50:14.990 --> 00:50:17.410
And then there's Uncle Al.
而且还有个阿尔叔叔。

1073
00:50:17.590 --> 00:50:18.810
But it's Elbert.
但确实是埃尔伯特。

1074
00:50:19.530 --> 00:50:20.050
Elbert.
埃尔伯特。

1075
00:50:20.310 --> 00:50:20.690
Correct.
没错。

1076
00:50:21.110 --> 00:50:21.610
Thank you.
谢谢。

1077
00:50:21.610 --> 00:50:29.030
Well, as the doors open, we reveal Phyllis in her wedding dress and Pam turns to camera
当大门打开，菲利斯穿着婚纱出现时，帕姆转向镜头

1078
00:50:29.030 --> 00:50:33.050
and says, oh, my God, that's my dress.
说，天哪，那是我的婚纱。

1079
00:50:33.930 --> 00:50:38.610
So she has stolen the invitations and now her wedding dress.
所以她不仅偷了请柬，现在连婚纱也偷了。

1080
00:50:38.850 --> 00:50:44.050
We had a fan question, Angela, from Kaylee Connelly, and I'm going to need your input here.
安吉拉，我们有个粉丝凯莉·康纳利的问题，我需要你发表一下看法。

1081
00:50:44.390 --> 00:50:44.470
OK.
好的。

1082
00:50:44.470 --> 00:50:51.730
She says throughout this episode, Pam realizes that Phyllis has stolen all of her wedding details.
她说在这一集中，帕姆意识到菲利斯偷走了她所有的婚礼细节。

1083
00:50:52.130 --> 00:50:54.690
And then she's wearing the same dress.
然后她还穿了同一件婚纱。

1084
00:50:55.010 --> 00:51:05.170
Well, in the season finale, Angela looks like she's wearing the same dress that Phyllis wore in her wedding to Dwight.
嗯，在季终集里，安吉拉看起来穿的也是菲利斯婚礼上穿的那件婚纱，那是为了德怀特穿的。

1085
00:51:05.170 --> 00:51:06.710
Wait, was this planned?
等等，这是计划好的吗？

1086
00:51:07.370 --> 00:51:07.750
OK.
好的。

1087
00:51:08.330 --> 00:51:10.210
So I wrote this down, too.
我也把这点记下来了。

1088
00:51:10.430 --> 00:51:13.250
You guys, when we were watching it, I was watching it with the kids.
伙计们，我们看的时候，我是和孩子们一起看的。

1089
00:51:13.350 --> 00:51:15.330
I said, oh, my gosh, that's my dress.
我说，天哪，那是我的裙子。

1090
00:51:15.990 --> 00:51:18.850
And then the kids were like, no, you mean it's Pam's dress.
然后孩子们说，不，你是说那是帕姆的裙子。

1091
00:51:18.970 --> 00:51:20.210
I said, no, it's my dress.
我说，不，那是我的裙子。

1092
00:51:20.850 --> 00:51:23.190
And I have all these photos on my phone.
我手机里还有所有这些照片。

1093
00:51:23.370 --> 00:51:28.310
I took a ton of photos for the finale, Jenna, of my wardrobe fitting, all of it.
珍娜，拍季终集的时候我拍了好多照片，关于我的服装试穿，所有的一切。

1094
00:51:28.870 --> 00:51:30.750
It is almost identical.
几乎一模一样。

1095
00:51:31.070 --> 00:51:33.310
I don't think this was planned, obviously.
我觉得这显然不是计划好的。

1096
00:51:33.310 --> 00:51:37.350
I don't think Angela Martin would try to emulate Phyllis's dress.
我不认为安吉拉·马丁会试图模仿菲利斯的裙子。

1097
00:51:37.650 --> 00:51:39.370
I think it was by chance.
我觉得这纯属巧合。

1098
00:51:39.810 --> 00:51:42.690
But you guys, it is so similar.
但是伙计们，真的太像了。

1099
00:51:42.870 --> 00:51:46.030
I had a little lace shawl jacket thing.
我当时穿了一件蕾丝披肩外套之类的东西。

1100
00:51:46.270 --> 00:51:47.690
It didn't come long sleeve.
它不是长袖的。

1101
00:51:47.890 --> 00:51:50.910
Like Phyllis's goes all the way to her wrists, you know.
菲利斯的袖子一直延伸到手腕，你知道的。

1102
00:51:51.090 --> 00:51:54.150
Mine went sort of just to the elbow area.
我的袖子大概只到手肘附近。

1103
00:51:54.350 --> 00:51:56.670
And then we had a strapless kind of dress.
然后我们穿的是那种抹胸裙。

1104
00:51:56.850 --> 00:51:59.970
I do not have a broad ribbon band on mine like hers.
我的裙子上没有像她那样宽的缎带。

1105
00:52:00.210 --> 00:52:01.870
But it's super similar.
但真的非常像。

1106
00:52:02.110 --> 00:52:03.110
I looked it up, too.
我也查过了。

1107
00:52:03.310 --> 00:52:06.470
I had pictures side by side on my computer.
我在电脑上把照片放在一起对比过。

1108
00:52:06.730 --> 00:52:10.930
They are so it's like the cut of the dress is so similar.
它们简直……裙子的剪裁太像了。

1109
00:52:11.130 --> 00:52:11.450
Crazy.
太疯狂了。

1110
00:52:11.670 --> 00:52:12.150
I know.
我知道。

1111
00:52:12.350 --> 00:52:14.190
OK, so they're walking down the aisle.
好了，他们正走在红毯上。

1112
00:52:14.390 --> 00:52:19.410
And as they get about halfway down, Albert is sort of moved to stand up.
当他们走到一半时，阿尔伯特似乎被感动得站了起来。

1113
00:52:19.530 --> 00:52:20.910
He's like he wants to try.
他好像想试着走一走。

1114
00:52:21.330 --> 00:52:21.470
Right.
没错。

1115
00:52:21.690 --> 00:52:22.990
It's his daughter's wedding.
那是他女儿的婚礼。

1116
00:52:23.310 --> 00:52:24.930
And Phyllis is so delighted.
菲利斯非常高兴。

1117
00:52:24.930 --> 00:52:28.410
She she just starts to smile and everyone applauds.
她开始微笑，大家都鼓起掌来。

1118
00:52:28.870 --> 00:52:31.550
And Michael is like, no freaking way.
而迈克尔却觉得，绝不可能。

1119
00:52:31.730 --> 00:52:33.310
He had one job.
他本来只有一项任务。

1120
00:52:33.510 --> 00:52:35.710
He had one job.
他本来只有一项任务。

1121
00:52:36.070 --> 00:52:37.770
And they just took it away from him.
结果他们就这样把它从他手里夺走了。

1122
00:52:38.350 --> 00:52:38.930
Yes.
是的。

1123
00:52:38.930 --> 00:52:45.450
And he just reverts back to that little boy who didn't get to walk down the aisle with the rings and the dog took his spot.
他又变回了那个没能拿着戒指走红毯、被狗抢了风头的小男孩。

1124
00:52:45.670 --> 00:52:51.390
So Michael is just watching Phyllis and her father walk down the aisle to all of this applause.
所以迈克尔就看着菲利斯和她父亲在掌声中走过红毯。

1125
00:52:51.390 --> 00:53:02.210
What he does is just sort of awkwardly pushes slash drags the wheelchair down the aisle behind them.
他做的事就是尴尬地推着或者说拖着轮椅跟在他们后面走。

1126
00:53:02.750 --> 00:53:05.290
So here's my question, Jenna, because you have the script.
所以珍娜，我有问题要问你，因为你有剧本。

1127
00:53:05.750 --> 00:53:10.390
I sort of figured in the script it would say Michael awkwardly walks behind them.
我本来以为剧本里会写迈克尔尴尬地跟在他们后面走。

1128
00:53:10.510 --> 00:53:11.990
Was that dragging of the wheelchair?
那个拖轮椅的动作？

1129
00:53:12.150 --> 00:53:14.130
Was that Steve or was that in the script?
那是史蒂夫自己加的，还是剧本里写的？

1130
00:53:14.890 --> 00:53:17.690
Oh, Angela, you are not the only person to wonder.
噢，安吉拉，不止你一个人好奇。

1131
00:53:17.870 --> 00:53:24.550
Oh, so I did look this up because Camille, Sarah, Dylan, Megan and Katie all asked the same question.
噢，我确实查过了，因为卡米尔、莎拉、迪伦、梅根和凯蒂都问了同样的问题。

1132
00:53:25.250 --> 00:53:27.650
Yes, it was scripted.
是的，那是剧本写的。

1133
00:53:27.830 --> 00:53:29.690
Here's what it says in the script.
剧本里是这么写的。

1134
00:53:29.690 --> 00:53:34.290
It says, Michael can't figure out how to undo the lock on the wheelchair.
上面写着，迈克尔不知道怎么解开轮椅的锁。

1135
00:53:34.290 --> 00:53:38.730
So he drags it down while still doing a traditional wedding walk.
所以他一边拖着轮椅，一边还要保持传统的婚礼步伐。

1136
00:53:39.290 --> 00:53:39.710
Amazing.
太绝了。

1137
00:53:40.510 --> 00:53:40.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1138
00:53:41.190 --> 00:53:45.090
So all of that of him doing the like step together, step together.
所以他那些“迈步、并拢，迈步、并拢”的动作。

1139
00:53:45.650 --> 00:53:48.730
That was, you know, a script note.
那你知道，是剧本里的备注。

1140
00:53:48.930 --> 00:53:50.910
Well, we asked Phyllis about this moment.
嗯，我们问过菲利斯关于这一幕的感受。

1141
00:53:50.990 --> 00:53:52.270
And here's what she had to say.
她是这么说的。

1142
00:53:52.590 --> 00:53:57.590
One of the scenes that stood out in my mind was when I was walking down the aisle.
我印象最深的一场戏是我走红毯的时候。

1143
00:53:57.590 --> 00:54:03.510
And since I've never been married, to me, that was a real thrill.
因为我从没结过婚，对我来说，那真的很令人激动。

1144
00:54:04.290 --> 00:54:07.310
And then Michael, Steve, Michael,
然后迈克尔，史蒂夫，迈克尔，

1145
00:54:07.610 --> 00:54:16.870
when he started dragging the wheelchair after my dad had gotten up and was going to walk me down the aisle and Michael was dragging the wheelchair,
当他在我爸爸站起来准备陪我走红毯后，开始拖着轮椅走的时候，

1146
00:54:17.850 --> 00:54:20.550
I could not keep a straight face.
我根本没法忍住不笑。

1147
00:54:20.670 --> 00:54:30.310
And I was so happy that the majority of the time my back was to that to that action because it was just hard to to keep it in.
我很庆幸大部分时间我的背是对着那个方向的，因为真的很难忍住。

1148
00:54:30.470 --> 00:54:33.890
Just the sound of the wheelchair dragging down the aisle.
光是听到轮椅在红毯上拖行的声音就够了。

1149
00:54:34.010 --> 00:54:34.970
I remember that.
我记得那个声音。

1150
00:54:35.150 --> 00:54:36.810
I remember it was very hard to get through.
我记得那场戏拍得非常艰难。

1151
00:54:37.050 --> 00:54:39.790
Jenna, I don't know if you remember, but I sat directly behind you.
珍娜，不知道你还记不记得，我当时就坐在你正后方。

1152
00:54:40.050 --> 00:54:40.290
No.
不记得。

1153
00:54:40.290 --> 00:54:44.530
Yes, and we were tickled because between scenes we could turn around and chat to each other.
记得的，我们当时还觉得挺逗，因为在拍摄间隙我们可以转过身来聊天。

1154
00:54:44.730 --> 00:54:52.730
Well, it's funny because someone pointed out that it seemed like all of the Dunder Mifflin employees were on one side except for Pam.
说来有趣，有人指出好像邓德·米夫林的所有员工都坐在同一侧，除了帕姆。

1155
00:54:53.110 --> 00:54:53.410
Yes.
没错。

1156
00:54:53.650 --> 00:54:55.790
Usually there's a bride's side and a groom's side.
通常婚礼会有新娘方和新郎方。

1157
00:54:55.930 --> 00:54:58.030
But I guess we sat on the groom's side.
但我猜我们是坐在新郎那一侧了。

1158
00:54:58.150 --> 00:55:02.670
But I do remember I have such a memory of how beautiful the back of your hair looked.
不过我确实记得，你当时脑后的发型看起来特别美，我记忆犹新。

1159
00:55:03.250 --> 00:55:04.750
It looks so beautiful.
看起来真美。

1160
00:55:05.250 --> 00:55:08.990
I watched this episode and I just thought I looked fantastic.
我看了这一集，心想自己当时看起来真是太棒了。

1161
00:55:08.990 --> 00:55:12.350
I'm just going to say, I was like, oh my gosh.
我只想说，我当时心想，天哪。

1162
00:55:12.450 --> 00:55:12.810
You did.
你确实很棒。

1163
00:55:12.890 --> 00:55:14.650
My hair looks amazing.
我的头发看起来太赞了。

1164
00:55:14.930 --> 00:55:18.230
That dress, that color, that chocolatey color dress.
还有那件裙子，那个颜色，那种巧克力色的裙子。

1165
00:55:18.390 --> 00:55:20.750
I'd never seen you in that color before, personally.
就我个人而言，我以前从没见你穿过那个颜色。

1166
00:55:20.750 --> 00:55:23.390
Why don't I wear that color more is what I thought.
我当时想的是，我为什么不多穿穿那个颜色呢。

1167
00:55:23.650 --> 00:55:24.330
I don't know.
我也不知道。

1168
00:55:24.510 --> 00:55:29.250
I feel like that color inspired me because that was the color of the dress I wore to the Golden Globes.
我觉得那个颜色启发了我，因为我参加金球奖时穿的裙子就是那个颜色。

1169
00:55:29.610 --> 00:55:32.430
Remember that time when we met Ben Affleck?
还记得我们遇见本·阿弗莱克那次吗？

1170
00:55:32.790 --> 00:55:32.910
Yeah.
记得。

1171
00:55:33.070 --> 00:55:33.470
Yes.
记得。

1172
00:55:34.970 --> 00:55:35.450
Yes.
记得。

1173
00:55:36.230 --> 00:55:38.610
I was like, if Pam can wear it, I can wear it.
我当时心想，如果帕姆能穿，那我也能穿。

1174
00:55:38.610 --> 00:55:41.830
Well, I noticed something else about the wedding guests.
对了，关于婚礼宾客我还注意到了别的事。

1175
00:55:42.210 --> 00:55:42.630
What?
什么事？

1176
00:55:43.210 --> 00:55:44.590
No Gino and Leo.
吉诺和里奥没来。

1177
00:55:45.590 --> 00:55:49.210
Bob Vance did not seem to invite any employees.
鲍勃·万斯好像没邀请任何员工。

1178
00:55:49.210 --> 00:55:51.870
So Phyllis invited all of her work friends.
菲利斯邀请了她所有的工作伙伴。

1179
00:55:51.990 --> 00:55:56.590
But I didn't see a big bunch of Vance refrigeration people.
但我没看到万斯制冷公司的一大群人。

1180
00:55:57.190 --> 00:55:59.690
Well, you only know two of them, really.
其实你也就认识他们两个而已。

1181
00:56:00.050 --> 00:56:00.690
Gino and Leo.
吉诺和里奥。

1182
00:56:01.250 --> 00:56:04.310
Maybe Phyllis was like, those two will do something.
也许菲利斯当时想的是，这两个人肯定会搞出点什么事来。

1183
00:56:04.350 --> 00:56:05.750
They're always up to something.
他们总是没安好心。

1184
00:56:05.750 --> 00:56:06.830
They're on my liSt.
他们上我的黑名单了。

1185
00:56:07.030 --> 00:56:07.950
They're on my no liSt.
他们被我拉黑了。

1186
00:56:08.710 --> 00:56:09.150
Yeah.
确实。

1187
00:56:09.390 --> 00:56:13.210
Well, I'm sure Bob was like, we're inviting Michael, but I can't bring Gino and Leo.
我觉得鲍勃当时肯定说，我们要邀请迈克尔，但我不能带上吉诺和里奥。

1188
00:56:13.510 --> 00:56:14.650
I don't think Bob cared.
我觉得鲍勃才不在乎呢。

1189
00:56:15.130 --> 00:56:19.950
Well, I don't know if you noticed in the line of groomsmen standing up there.
对了，不知道你有没有注意到站在那儿的一排伴郎。

1190
00:56:20.210 --> 00:56:21.890
There are a set of twins.
里面有一对双胞胎。

1191
00:56:23.150 --> 00:56:25.450
Those are meant to be Bob's grown sons.
他们设定是鲍勃成年的儿子。

1192
00:56:26.270 --> 00:56:26.650
Oh.
噢。

1193
00:56:27.030 --> 00:56:31.270
It's in the script that Bob's twin sons are standing up for him.
剧本里写着鲍勃的双胞胎儿子在为他担任伴郎。

1194
00:56:31.370 --> 00:56:37.390
So he has his best friend and who gives a little bit of a speech later and then his twin sons.
所以他有他的好朋友——后来还发表了一小段演讲——然后就是他的双胞胎儿子。

1195
00:56:37.550 --> 00:56:41.530
And then I don't know who the other man is meant to be, but no Gino and Leo.
至于另一个人是谁我就不知道了，但反正没有吉诺和里奥。

1196
00:56:42.190 --> 00:56:44.150
So Phyllis is now a stepmom.
所以菲利斯现在是继母了。

1197
00:56:44.670 --> 00:56:45.050
Yeah.
没错。

1198
00:56:45.650 --> 00:56:51.550
The minister is trying to finish the vows, but Michael jumps the gun and he pronounces
牧师正准备完成誓词，但迈克尔抢先一步宣布了

1199
00:56:51.550 --> 00:56:53.210
Bob and Phyllis man and wife.
鲍勃和菲利斯结为夫妻。

1200
00:56:53.630 --> 00:56:55.210
He had to get something in there.
他总得在那儿插上一脚。

1201
00:56:55.330 --> 00:56:58.930
And it's crickets because the vows aren't finished, everyone.
大家安静了，因为誓词还没念完呢，各位。

1202
00:56:59.350 --> 00:57:02.770
You know what the best job for Michael would have been is if he could have just been the
你们知道迈克尔最适合的工作是什么吗，如果他能当个

1203
00:57:02.770 --> 00:57:04.370
DJ at the reception.
婚宴上的DJ就好了。

1204
00:57:04.530 --> 00:57:06.890
Just be the person who announces them in.
只要负责把他们介绍出场就行。

1205
00:57:06.990 --> 00:57:10.570
For the first time, I'd like to introduce to you.
“现在，我想向大家隆重介绍……”

1206
00:57:10.990 --> 00:57:12.550
Yes, that could have been it.
没错，本来可以是这样的。

1207
00:57:12.910 --> 00:57:13.810
Give him a microphone.
给他个麦克风。

1208
00:57:14.170 --> 00:57:16.810
It would be like the Dundies for him all over again.
对他来说就像重温了一次邓迪奖颁奖礼。

1209
00:57:16.910 --> 00:57:19.530
He could be like, and now for the first dance and all of that.
他可以像这样：“现在，有请新人跳第一支舞”，诸如此类。

1210
00:57:19.750 --> 00:57:20.450
Well, I don't know.
嗯，我不知道。

1211
00:57:20.570 --> 00:57:24.070
I don't know if you should give Michael a microphone as we will see soon.
我不知道你该不该给迈克尔麦克风，我们很快就会看到了。

1212
