是啊。

1673
01:17:48.330 --> 01:17:48.730
Yes.
我想拉什达如果知道阿里安娜·诺文伯写信来问“拉什达·琼斯是受过训练的歌手吗？”一定会很开心。

1674
01:17:49.050 --> 01:17:54.590
And I think Rashida would be happy to know that Ariana November wrote in to say, is Rashida
因为她唱得真的很好。

1675
01:17:54.590 --> 01:17:56.070
Jones a trained singer?
我也觉得她的嗓音很棒。

1676
01:17:56.070 --> 01:17:57.770
Because she is really good.
我也是。

1677
01:17:58.150 --> 01:18:00.110
And I thought she had a great voice, too.
我也是。

1678
01:18:00.130 --> 01:18:00.870
I did, too.
然后我甚至觉得，吉姆的反应，比如在空中挥舞手机。

1679
01:18:01.150 --> 01:18:01.770
I did, too.
那很可爱。

1680
01:18:01.910 --> 01:18:05.290
And then I even thought, you know, Jim's reaction, like waving his phone in the air.
是啊。

1681
01:18:05.290 --> 01:18:06.450
It was cute.
接着菲利斯扔出了捧花，瑞安把它从凯莉手里拍开了。

1682
01:18:07.350 --> 01:18:07.870
Yeah.
凯莉显然是想接住那束捧花的，但瑞安把它拍开了。

1683
01:18:08.690 --> 01:18:15.730
So then Phyllis tosses her bouquet and Ryan swats it away from Kelly.
很多人想知道那是不是剧本安排的。

1684
01:18:16.010 --> 01:18:19.770
Kelly was clearly going to catch that bouquet and Ryan swats it away.
是的。

1685
01:18:20.010 --> 01:18:23.770
A lot of people wanted to know if that was a scripted moment.
是的，是剧本安排的。

1686
01:18:24.270 --> 01:18:24.650
Yes.
瑞安不能让凯莉接到捧花。

1687
01:18:25.190 --> 01:18:26.010
Yes, it was.
你知道那会对他们的关系造成什么影响吗？

1688
01:18:26.410 --> 01:18:27.970
Ryan can't let Kelly catch that.
不，不，不。

1689
01:18:28.150 --> 01:18:29.950
Do you know what that would do for their relationship?
但最后是谁接到了呢？

1690
01:18:29.950 --> 01:18:30.750
No, no, no.
托比的女伴。

1691
01:18:30.910 --> 01:18:32.170
But who does catch it?
珍娜，我特别喜欢托比对着镜头的那个单人采访，他说，托比，耶。

1692
01:18:32.970 --> 01:18:33.870
Toby's date.
是啊。

1693
01:18:33.890 --> 01:18:39.570
And I loved so much, Jenna, that one-on-one of Toby to camera where he's like, Toby, yeah.
好了，现在我们转到外面，迈克尔正和阿尔叔叔坐在长椅上。

1694
01:18:39.990 --> 01:18:40.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1695
01:18:41.070 --> 01:18:46.410
Well, now we move outside and Michael is sitting on a bench with Uncle Al.
他们正在进行一场推心置腹的谈话。

1696
01:18:46.610 --> 01:18:46.730
Yeah.
那有多完美啊？

1697
01:18:46.850 --> 01:18:48.770
And they're having this big heart-to-heart.
噢。

1698
01:18:48.850 --> 01:18:49.850
How perfect is that?
那真是一个很棒的场景。

1699
01:18:50.690 --> 01:18:51.170
Oh.
是啊。

1700
01:18:52.070 --> 01:18:54.110
It was such a great scene.
那真是一个很棒的场景。

1701
01:18:54.330 --> 01:18:56.310
We had some people write in.
我们收到了一些观众的来信。

1702
01:18:56.650 --> 01:19:05.450
Christy Carroll, Connor Yakes, and Ashley Howell all asked, can you talk about the actors that played Uncle Al and Phyllis' dad, Elbert?
Christy Carroll、Connor Yakes 和 Ashley Howell 都问，能不能聊聊饰演阿尔叔叔和菲利斯父亲埃尔伯特的演员？

1703
01:19:05.610 --> 01:19:07.230
Because they were both fabulous.
因为他们俩都太棒了。

1704
01:19:07.230 --> 01:19:14.470
Well, guys, George Ives played Uncle Al, and he was a longtime television actor.
好吧，伙计们，乔治·艾夫斯饰演了阿尔叔叔，他是一位资深的电视演员。

1705
01:19:14.790 --> 01:19:21.890
He appeared in Mr. Ed, The Andy Griffith Show, My Three Sons, Bewitched, and a bunch of movies.
他出演过《艾德先生》、《安迪·格里菲斯秀》、《我的三个儿子》、《神仙俏女巫》以及许多电影。

1706
01:19:22.190 --> 01:19:30.510
He passed away in 2013, and The Office was his last television show that he appeared in, according to IMDb.
他于2013年去世，据 IMDb 显示，《办公室》是他出演的最后一部电视剧。

1707
01:19:31.270 --> 01:19:31.910
Yeah.
没错。

1708
01:19:32.050 --> 01:19:34.230
And he was just absolutely fabulous.
他真的非常出色。

1709
01:19:36.330 --> 01:19:40.150
And then Hansford Rowe played Phyllis' father.
然后是汉斯福德·罗饰演了菲利斯的父亲。

1710
01:19:40.410 --> 01:19:42.670
He passed away in 2017.
他于2017年去世。

1711
01:19:43.330 --> 01:19:46.370
He was a very accomplished actor.
他是一位非常有成就的演员。

1712
01:19:47.030 --> 01:19:48.870
Listen to the movies he's been in.
听听他演过的电影。

1713
01:19:49.070 --> 01:19:53.570
He was in Dante's Peak, Baby Boom, Three Days of the Condor.
他出演过《但丁峰》、《婴儿炸弹》、《秃鹰七十二小时》。

1714
01:19:53.750 --> 01:20:00.270
He's been in a ton of television shows, Modern Family, Will and Grace, Curb Your Enthusiasm, Six Feet Under.
他还出演过大量的电视剧，比如《摩登家庭》、《威尔和格蕾丝》、《抑制热情》、《六尺之下》。

1715
01:20:00.530 --> 01:20:02.210
But here's the one that got me.
但下面这个让我震惊。

1716
01:20:02.210 --> 01:20:06.590
He was in this miniseries called V.
他出演过一部叫《V》的迷你剧。

1717
01:20:07.570 --> 01:20:08.870
Do you remember V?
你还记得《V》吗？

1718
01:20:09.410 --> 01:20:11.890
Was it about aliens taking over?
是关于外星人入侵的那部吗？

1719
01:20:12.730 --> 01:20:13.230
Yes.
是的。

1720
01:20:13.230 --> 01:20:13.870
And then you would.
那你肯定记得。

1721
01:20:14.110 --> 01:20:15.050
It was from the 80s.
那是80年代的剧。

1722
01:20:15.230 --> 01:20:18.270
Yeah, people would do the sign, the V, the little sign with their fingers.
没错，人们会做那个手势，那个用手指比出的 V 字。

1723
01:20:18.430 --> 01:20:18.490
Yes.
是的。

1724
01:20:18.490 --> 01:20:18.710
Yeah.
没错。

1725
01:20:20.770 --> 01:20:26.650
And the way you found out they were aliens is they would peel off their skin and they were like lizard people underneath.
你发现他们是外星人的方式是，他们会剥掉皮肤，下面是蜥蜴人。

1726
01:20:26.890 --> 01:20:26.990
Yeah.
没错。

1727
01:20:27.090 --> 01:20:27.770
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1728
01:20:27.770 --> 01:20:29.450
I forgot about that show.
我把那部剧给忘了。

1729
01:20:30.170 --> 01:20:32.970
Remember how shocking it was when you saw their lizard skin?
还记得看到他们蜥蜴皮肤时有多震惊吗？

1730
01:20:32.970 --> 01:20:33.250
Yeah.
记得。

1731
01:20:33.450 --> 01:20:40.010
Well, listen, we had a fan question from Sierra, Katie Regan, Katie Slemp, Allison and Lexi.
好了，听着，我们收到了来自 Sierra、Katie Regan、Katie Slemp、Allison 和 Lexi 的粉丝提问。

1732
01:20:40.010 --> 01:20:48.930
They all noticed that at 19 minutes, 30 seconds, as Phyllis is leaving the church, she seems to have a black brace on her right knee.
她们都注意到在19分30秒时，菲利斯离开教堂时，她的右膝盖上似乎戴着一个黑色护具。

1733
01:20:50.530 --> 01:20:54.910
Well, guys, I asked Phyllis about this and she does not remember.
伙计们，我问过菲利斯这件事，她不记得了。

1734
01:20:55.150 --> 01:20:58.790
She was definitely not injured during the making of this episode.
她在拍摄这一集时绝对没有受伤。

1735
01:20:59.130 --> 01:21:04.210
But, you know, she said she went through a few injuries during her time on the show.
但她说，她在剧组期间确实受过几次伤。

1736
01:21:04.210 --> 01:21:08.430
And I guess this must have been when she was favoring that knee a little bit.
我猜这一定是因为当时她的膝盖有点不舒服。

1737
01:21:08.570 --> 01:21:09.650
But I stopped it.
但我暂停看了看。

1738
01:21:09.750 --> 01:21:12.250
And sure enough, there is a little bit of a bandage there.
果然，那里确实有一点绷带。

1739
01:21:12.430 --> 01:21:14.110
I did not catch that.
我没注意到。

1740
01:21:14.690 --> 01:21:15.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1741
01:21:15.470 --> 01:21:15.930
Oh, man.
天呐。

1742
01:21:15.930 --> 01:21:18.990
We have really good background catchers that watch the show.
我们有非常厉害的背景细节捕捉者在看这部剧。

1743
01:21:18.990 --> 01:21:19.390
We do.
确实。

1744
01:21:19.610 --> 01:21:22.390
Well, now we have this tag, this little scene at the end.
好了，现在是片尾彩蛋，最后那个小场景。

1745
01:21:22.530 --> 01:21:23.990
And it's Bob and Phyllis.
是鲍勃和菲利斯。

1746
01:21:24.130 --> 01:21:28.550
They're doing that thing where you shove the wedding cake in the face kind of thing.
他们正在做那种把婚礼蛋糕往对方脸上抹的事情。

1747
01:21:28.710 --> 01:21:30.590
And, of course, Michael wants to get in on it.
当然，迈克尔也想掺和一脚。

1748
01:21:30.590 --> 01:21:31.610
It's really awkward.
真的很尴尬。

1749
01:21:31.910 --> 01:21:33.830
I don't know if you noticed on this cake.
不知道你们有没有注意到这个蛋糕。

1750
01:21:33.830 --> 01:21:35.070
It was so amazing.
它太惊人了。

1751
01:21:35.370 --> 01:21:36.170
It was so well done.
做得太棒了。

1752
01:21:36.290 --> 01:21:42.110
There was a full silver refrigerator made of fondant that sat on top of the cake.
蛋糕顶上放着一个用翻糖做的银色冰箱。

1753
01:21:42.110 --> 01:21:45.910
It's like the topper next to the little bride and groom figurine.
就像新郎新娘小人偶旁边的装饰物一样。

1754
01:21:46.050 --> 01:21:47.230
I did not notice that.
我没注意到那个。

1755
01:21:47.390 --> 01:21:47.650
Yes.
是的。

1756
01:21:47.810 --> 01:21:49.150
That is brilliant.
那真是太绝了。

1757
01:21:49.630 --> 01:21:50.150
Of course.
当然。

1758
01:21:50.350 --> 01:21:54.750
Of course there was a Vance refrigerator on the top of the cake with them.
蛋糕顶上当然放着一个万斯冰箱，和他们在一起。

1759
01:21:54.830 --> 01:21:55.850
That was also cake.
那也是蛋糕做的。

1760
01:21:56.150 --> 01:22:01.210
So you know how you take the top part of the cake and you save it and you have it on your one year anniversary?
你知道那种把蛋糕顶层留下来，等到结婚一周年纪念日再吃掉的习俗吗？

1761
01:22:01.870 --> 01:22:02.270
Yeah.
知道。

1762
01:22:02.290 --> 01:22:03.590
They're going to eat that refrigerator.
他们打算把那个冰箱吃掉。

1763
01:22:04.910 --> 01:22:06.470
Their one year anniversary.
在他们结婚一周年纪念日那天。

1764
01:22:08.050 --> 01:22:09.030
Did you do that?
你当时这么做了吗？

1765
01:22:09.210 --> 01:22:11.490
Did you save the top of your cake and eat it a year later?
你留下了蛋糕顶层，一年后把它吃掉了吗？

1766
01:22:11.670 --> 01:22:11.910
No.
没有。

1767
01:22:12.610 --> 01:22:13.090
Did you?
你呢？

1768
01:22:13.170 --> 01:22:13.490
Oh, no.
哦，没有。

1769
01:22:13.510 --> 01:22:13.890
Did you?
你呢？

1770
01:22:14.070 --> 01:22:14.590
You know what?
你知道吗？

1771
01:22:14.630 --> 01:22:15.090
It's weird.
这很奇怪。

1772
01:22:15.290 --> 01:22:16.370
I can't remember.
我不记得了。

1773
01:22:16.370 --> 01:22:23.450
But this past year, we just celebrated our 10th wedding anniversary, Lee and I, 10 years this year.
但就在过去这一年，我和李刚庆祝了我们的结婚十周年纪念日，今年正好十年。

1774
01:22:23.630 --> 01:22:24.950
That's amazing, lady.
太棒了，亲爱的。

1775
01:22:24.950 --> 01:22:27.870
Well, and it happened during a pandemic.
嗯，而且这还是在疫情期间发生的。

1776
01:22:28.130 --> 01:22:38.670
And we had these plans that for our 10th wedding anniversary, we wanted to take a big trip and take the kids to the spot where Lee proposed to me.
我们原本计划在结婚十周年纪念日时去旅行，带孩子们去李向我求婚的地方。

1777
01:22:38.670 --> 01:22:42.810
And I wanted to have a family portrait taken in this spot.
我还想在那个地方拍一张全家福。

1778
01:22:42.810 --> 01:22:48.170
Oh, and that was I mean, I've been had this in my head for like years since our seventh wedding anniversary.
哦，那是……我是说，从我们结婚七周年开始，我就一直有这个想法。

1779
01:22:48.170 --> 01:22:51.590
Yes, that this would be such a fun way to mark our 10th wedding anniversary.
是的，觉得这将是纪念我们结婚十周年的有趣方式。

1780
01:22:51.590 --> 01:22:57.150
Well, you know, then we couldn't really go anywhere because our our anniversary is in July.
嗯，你知道，后来我们哪儿也去不了，因为我们的纪念日在七月。

1781
01:22:57.190 --> 01:23:05.190
So we ended up having dinner outside underneath our fruit trees and our original wedding planner, Beth Helmstetter.
所以我们最后在果树下的户外吃了晚餐，我们的婚礼策划师贝丝·赫尔姆斯泰特（Beth Helmstetter）——

1782
01:23:05.390 --> 01:23:05.870
You know her.
你认识她。

1783
01:23:07.070 --> 01:23:09.270
She set it all up for us.
她为我们安排好了一切。

1784
01:23:09.450 --> 01:23:10.210
She came over.
她过来了。

1785
01:23:10.410 --> 01:23:11.470
She wore a mask.
她戴着口罩。

1786
01:23:11.630 --> 01:23:15.290
She set this little table out under our trees.
她在树下摆了一张小桌子。

1787
01:23:15.510 --> 01:23:16.890
And do you know what she did for us?
你知道她为我们做了什么吗？

1788
01:23:17.070 --> 01:23:17.190
What?
什么？

1789
01:23:17.430 --> 01:23:30.210
She had the records from our wedding and she had a tiny replica of our wedding cake made for us for four people so that our kids could eat our wedding cake on our 10th wedding anniversary.
她找来了我们婚礼上的唱片，还为我们定制了一个四人份的婚礼蛋糕微缩模型，这样我们的孩子们就能在结婚十周年纪念日那天吃上我们的婚礼蛋糕了。

1790
01:23:30.650 --> 01:23:31.350
That is so special.
那太特别了。

1791
01:23:31.810 --> 01:23:32.690
That is so sweet.
那太贴心了。

1792
01:23:32.690 --> 01:23:36.590
I wanted to tell you, though, we didn't eat the top of our cake.
不过我想告诉你，我们并没有吃掉蛋糕顶层。

1793
01:23:36.750 --> 01:23:39.390
That wasn't the type of cake we had at our wedding.
那不是我们婚礼上那种类型的蛋糕。

1794
01:23:39.390 --> 01:23:44.470
But I have to tell you our topper story, which is, you know, we're a blended family.
但我必须告诉你我们的蛋糕装饰故事，你知道，我们是一个重组家庭。

1795
01:23:44.690 --> 01:23:46.510
We were two whole families coming together.
我们是两个完整的家庭走到了一起。

1796
01:23:46.570 --> 01:23:49.470
So our children were a really big part of our wedding.
所以我们的孩子们在婚礼中扮演了非常重要的角色。

1797
01:23:49.850 --> 01:23:51.970
They all wanted to speak at the ceremony.
他们都想在仪式上发言。

1798
01:23:52.490 --> 01:24:02.290
And then when it came time for the cake, instead of getting a traditional bride and groom figurine, we let the kids design this out of Legos.
后来到了切蛋糕的时候，我们没有用传统的新郎新娘人偶，而是让孩子们用乐高积木设计了一个。

1799
01:24:03.310 --> 01:24:04.630
Oh, that's right.
哦，我想起来了。

1800
01:24:04.630 --> 01:24:11.470
And so we had a little Lego, sort of like they made like a little archway out of Legos.
所以我们有一个小乐高装饰，他们用乐高搭了一个小拱门。

1801
01:24:11.630 --> 01:24:14.330
And then they put little Lego flowers on the white archway.
然后在白色拱门上放了乐高小花。

1802
01:24:14.490 --> 01:24:18.630
And then they made Legos of me and Josh and then of each of them.
然后他们做了我和乔什的乐高人偶，还有他们每个人的。

1803
01:24:18.790 --> 01:24:19.630
So all three kids.
所以是三个孩子。

1804
01:24:19.630 --> 01:24:24.030
So we had five little Legos under a Lego archway on top of our wedding cake.
所以我们的婚礼蛋糕顶部的乐高拱门下有五个乐高小人。

1805
01:24:25.190 --> 01:24:25.790
So sweet.
太甜了。

1806
01:24:26.010 --> 01:24:26.310
So cute.
太可爱了。

1807
01:24:26.450 --> 01:24:26.570
Right.
没错。

1808
01:24:26.650 --> 01:24:27.330
And we saved it.
我们把它留下来了。

1809
01:24:27.430 --> 01:24:28.090
It's on our mantle.
就放在我们的壁炉架上。

1810
01:24:28.470 --> 01:24:29.990
Well, lady, I just love all that.
天哪，女士，我太喜欢这些了。

1811
01:24:30.230 --> 01:24:33.090
So we did get some questions about this cake scene.
关于这个蛋糕场景，我们确实收到了一些提问。

1812
01:24:33.250 --> 01:24:34.550
And guys, I want to let you know.
伙计们，我想告诉你们。

1813
01:24:34.550 --> 01:24:39.350
So this was originally shot to be earlier in the episode.
这段戏最初是打算放在剧集前段拍摄的。

1814
01:24:39.350 --> 01:24:41.110
And then they just liked it.
后来他们很喜欢这段。

1815
01:24:41.230 --> 01:24:42.590
So they used it as the tag.
所以就把它用作了片尾彩蛋。

1816
01:24:42.710 --> 01:24:49.950
But it was meant to go right before Dwight confronts Uncle Al for stealing the bread at the buffet and throws him out.
但它本该放在德怀特质问阿尔叔叔在自助餐偷面包并把他赶出去之前。

1817
01:24:49.950 --> 01:24:53.370
Well, there were some questions about why this was at the end of the episode.
嗯，有人问为什么这段放在了剧集结尾。

1818
01:24:53.570 --> 01:24:55.390
It was just sometimes we do that.
只是有时候我们会这么做。

1819
01:24:55.630 --> 01:25:00.330
Sometimes, you know, we cut back to a moment that might have happened earlier as our tag.
有时候，你知道的，我们会把之前发生过的一个片段剪辑回来作为彩蛋。

1820
01:25:00.350 --> 01:25:02.590
Well, that's the fun thing about a cold open and a tag.
这就是开场戏和片尾彩蛋的有趣之处。

1821
01:25:02.730 --> 01:25:06.270
Sometimes they don't have to be in sort of a time ordered manner.
有时候它们不必按时间顺序排列。

1822
01:25:07.170 --> 01:25:07.610
Yes.
是的。

1823
01:25:08.070 --> 01:25:08.510
Yes.
没错。

1824
01:25:09.150 --> 01:25:19.010
Well, the original tag of this episode was supposed to be a series of photos where Michael is photo bombing every single picture.
其实这集最初的彩蛋是一系列照片，迈克尔在每一张照片里都乱入抢镜。

1825
01:25:19.950 --> 01:25:22.430
I remember taking these pictures and you can find some of them.
我记得拍过这些照片，你们能找到其中的一些。

1826
01:25:22.590 --> 01:25:22.910
You can.
可以的。

1827
01:25:23.170 --> 01:25:23.610
Where are they?
它们在哪？

1828
01:25:23.690 --> 01:25:24.530
Office tally, maybe?
也许在《办公室》的统计网站上？

1829
01:25:24.750 --> 01:25:24.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1830
01:25:25.070 --> 01:25:29.550
So for a while, NBC had these photos up on their website.
有一段时间，NBC把这些照片放在了他们的官网上。

1831
01:25:29.950 --> 01:25:31.810
And I don't think they're there anymore.
我觉得现在应该不在了。

1832
01:25:31.810 --> 01:25:33.290
But I'm going to do a little digging.
但我会去挖一挖。

1833
01:25:33.290 --> 01:25:35.470
And if we can find them, we'll put them up on the pod.
如果我们能找到，我们会把它们发到播客上。

1834
01:25:35.750 --> 01:25:37.210
But I remember shooting them.
但我记得拍摄的过程。

1835
01:25:37.290 --> 01:25:38.230
It was very, very fun.
非常非常有趣。

1836
01:25:38.350 --> 01:25:38.570
Yeah.
是啊。

1837
01:25:38.570 --> 01:25:39.770
I remember those, too.
我也记得那些。

1838
01:25:40.150 --> 01:25:47.430
Well, you know, Jenna, we asked Phyllis about the cake and just about this episode, things she remembered and things that stood out to her.
嗯，你知道吗，珍娜，我们问了菲利斯关于蛋糕的事，还有关于这一集，她记得什么以及什么让她印象深刻。

1839
01:25:47.610 --> 01:25:48.750
And here's what she had to say.
这是她要说的。

1840
01:25:48.750 --> 01:25:51.210
Yes, it was very good cake.
是的，那蛋糕非常好吃。

1841
01:25:51.570 --> 01:25:54.610
And we didn't really do that many takes of it.
我们其实没拍多少次。

1842
01:25:54.690 --> 01:25:55.750
It was the end of the night.
那是那天晚上的最后一场戏了。

1843
01:25:55.750 --> 01:25:58.690
They didn't want to mess my face and hair up every time.
他们不想每次都弄乱我的妆发。

1844
01:25:58.690 --> 01:26:03.630
So I think we just practiced it without messing it all over our faces.
所以我记得我们只是练习了一下，没有把蛋糕弄得满脸都是。

1845
01:26:03.630 --> 01:26:06.110
And then we did it just the one time.
然后我们就拍了一次。

1846
01:26:06.630 --> 01:26:11.590
So, no, we didn't do that multiple times where it had to be cleaned up and this and that.
所以，不，我们没有拍很多次，不需要清理什么的。

1847
01:26:11.590 --> 01:26:17.670
And then Michael went crazy, of course, smearing it all over his face.
当然，后来迈克尔疯了，把蛋糕抹得满脸都是。

1848
01:26:17.670 --> 01:26:18.630
And, you know,
而且，你知道，

1849
01:26:18.870 --> 01:26:32.850
one of the funniest scenes that I think that tore me up when I saw it for the first time was when Michael was outside jumping at the window trying to look in after he had been escorted out by Dwight.
我觉得最搞笑的场景之一，第一次看的时候就把我笑坏了，就是迈克尔被德怀特赶出去后，在窗外跳着想往里看的时候。

1850
01:26:32.850 --> 01:26:36.250
And I don't know, for some reason, that just really tore me up.
我不知道为什么，那一幕真的让我笑得不行。

1851
01:26:36.370 --> 01:26:41.830
I thought that whole wedding was, of course I would, was a remarkable episode.
我觉得整场婚礼，当然我肯定会这么想，是一个非常精彩的片段。

1852
01:26:42.650 --> 01:26:46.830
Everybody had their shining moments in it.
每个人在里面都有闪光时刻。

1853
01:26:46.830 --> 01:26:56.490
Kelly dressed in white and the whole Pam and Jim, Karen, Roy Triangle, that was all great.
凯莉穿上白裙，还有帕姆、吉姆、凯伦和罗伊的三角关系，这一切都很棒。

1854
01:26:56.770 --> 01:26:58.550
It was just pretty special.
这真的很特别。

1855
01:26:59.050 --> 01:27:02.770
And Ken, I think Ken directed that.
还有肯，我觉得是肯执导的那一集。

1856
01:27:02.930 --> 01:27:04.190
He was fantastic.
他太棒了。

1857
01:27:04.190 --> 01:27:06.470
I always enjoyed working with him.
我一直很喜欢和他合作。

1858
01:27:06.670 --> 01:27:09.130
And we were so blessed on that show.
我们在那部剧里真是太幸运了。

1859
01:27:09.130 --> 01:27:17.690
We had so many great writers, directors, and the fact that we all got to grow up together on this show, basically.
我们有那么多优秀的编剧和导演，而且事实上，我们基本上是一起在那部剧里成长起来的。

1860
01:27:18.630 --> 01:27:22.010
Not just this episode, the whole nine seasons.
不仅仅是这一集，而是整整九季。

1861
01:27:22.930 --> 01:27:28.190
And it was really a blessing then and continues to be to this day.
那在当时真的是一种福分，直到今天依然如此。

1862
01:27:28.390 --> 01:27:29.990
I'm glad you enjoyed the episode.
很高兴你喜欢这一集。

1863
01:27:30.010 --> 01:27:31.490
I'm assuming you did.
我猜你是喜欢的。

1864
01:27:31.890 --> 01:27:34.330
And I'll talk to you later.
那我们回头再聊。

1865
01:27:34.950 --> 01:27:37.030
Well, now we're wrapping up the episode.
好了，现在我们要结束这一集了。

1866
01:27:37.030 --> 01:27:40.930
But, Jenna, before we say goodbye, I have to talk about a few deleted scenes.
但是，珍娜，在我们说再见之前，我得聊聊几个删减片段。

1867
01:27:41.290 --> 01:27:45.690
One I talked about with Ken Whittingham about Angela's whole runner with Dennis.
其中一个我和肯·惠廷汉姆聊过，关于安吉拉和丹尼斯的那条故事线。

1868
01:27:46.490 --> 01:27:46.970
Yes.
是的。

1869
01:27:46.970 --> 01:27:48.570
Dennis, the veterinarian.
丹尼斯，那个兽医。

1870
01:27:50.030 --> 01:27:50.510
Yes.
没错。

1871
01:27:50.510 --> 01:27:52.670
Who she says, I'm sorry, but I'm with someone.
她说，抱歉，但我已经有对象了。

1872
01:27:52.890 --> 01:27:54.830
She does end up turning Dennis down.
她最终确实拒绝了丹尼斯。

1873
01:27:55.030 --> 01:27:58.990
But here are the two other deleted scenes that were so funny to me.
但这里还有另外两个我觉得特别好笑的删减片段。

1874
01:27:59.350 --> 01:28:01.810
Number one, Kevin has a talking head.
第一，凯文有一个采访镜头。

1875
01:28:02.090 --> 01:28:06.430
He says that he has proposed to four different girls.
他说他向四个不同的女孩求过婚。

1876
01:28:07.070 --> 01:28:08.210
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1877
01:28:08.490 --> 01:28:08.630
Four.
四个。

1878
01:28:09.090 --> 01:28:12.450
But Stacey was the first one to say yes.
但史黛西是第一个答应的。

1879
01:28:12.790 --> 01:28:17.890
And, you know, if it couldn't be Melissa Riley, then he's glad it was Stacey.
而且，你知道，如果不是梅丽莎·莱利的话，他很高兴是史黛西。

1880
01:28:18.310 --> 01:28:18.490
Wow.
哇。

1881
01:28:18.510 --> 01:28:20.090
Who the heck is Melissa Riley?
梅丽莎·莱利到底是谁啊？

1882
01:28:20.830 --> 01:28:21.930
I don't know.
我不知道。

1883
01:28:22.210 --> 01:28:22.390
Okay.
好吧。

1884
01:28:22.390 --> 01:28:23.410
I thought that was delicious.
我觉得这太有意思了。

1885
01:28:23.730 --> 01:28:26.310
And this is the other one I loved.
还有这个我也很喜欢。

1886
01:28:26.590 --> 01:28:28.270
Wedding planners, listen up.
婚礼策划师们，听好了。

1887
01:28:28.270 --> 01:28:37.730
There is a deleted scene where Meredith holds up a party favor, and it's a little tiny refrigerator magnet.
有一个删减片段是梅雷迪斯举起一个伴手礼，那是一个小小的冰箱贴。

1888
01:28:38.090 --> 01:28:43.450
And when you open the door to the refrigerator, there's a picture of Phyllis and Bob.
当你打开冰箱门时，里面有菲利斯和鲍勃的照片。

1889
01:28:43.790 --> 01:28:44.290
Wow.
哇。

1890
01:28:44.630 --> 01:28:44.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1891
01:28:45.090 --> 01:28:47.610
Well, she didn't steal that from Pam's wedding.
好吧，她没从帕姆的婚礼上偷那个。

1892
01:28:47.810 --> 01:28:49.170
She didn't steal that one.
那个她没偷。

1893
01:28:49.290 --> 01:28:52.870
But don't you wish you had that magnet, that little refrigerator magnet?
难道你不想要那个冰箱贴吗，那个小小的冰箱贴？

1894
01:28:53.470 --> 01:28:56.590
So, in the deleted scene, we see this item?
所以，在那个删减片段里，我们看到了这个东西？

1895
01:28:57.090 --> 01:28:57.610
Yes.
是的。

1896
01:28:57.610 --> 01:28:59.010
I took a screen grab of it.
我截了张图。

1897
01:28:59.830 --> 01:29:01.430
Who has that now?
现在谁有那个东西？

1898
01:29:01.430 --> 01:29:02.270
I don't know.
我不知道。

1899
01:29:02.350 --> 01:29:04.450
But Meredith is the one who holds it up.
但梅雷迪斯是拿着它的人。

1900
01:29:04.590 --> 01:29:06.770
She's like, did you guys get your little magnet?
她当时说，你们拿到你们的小磁铁了吗？

1901
01:29:07.170 --> 01:29:08.570
And it's a refrigerator.
而且它是个冰箱。

1902
01:29:08.990 --> 01:29:09.950
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

1903
01:29:10.250 --> 01:29:15.750
Angela, I love this refrigerator magnet that goes on your refrigerator so much.
安吉拉，我太喜欢你冰箱上贴的那个冰箱贴了。

1904
01:29:16.530 --> 01:29:19.830
That I would like you, please, because you're in charge of our merch.
所以我有个请求，因为你是负责周边商品的。

1905
01:29:20.110 --> 01:29:20.450
I am.
没错，是我。

1906
01:29:20.530 --> 01:29:21.250
I love it, you guys.
伙计们，我太喜欢它了。

1907
01:29:21.250 --> 01:29:22.870
If you ever have ideas, let me know.
如果你们有什么想法，随时告诉我。

1908
01:29:23.210 --> 01:29:33.290
Well, I have one, so I'm letting you know, will you please make a refrigerator magnet with a little door that opens, and inside the refrigerator is me and you.
好吧，我正好有一个，现在就告诉你，能不能请你做一个冰箱贴，带有一扇能打开的小门，冰箱里面是我们俩。

1909
01:29:34.330 --> 01:29:36.050
I don't know why we're in the refrigerator.
我不知道为什么我们要待在冰箱里。

1910
01:29:36.690 --> 01:29:38.050
I just want to be in there.
我就是想待在里面。

1911
01:29:38.190 --> 01:29:38.590
Okay?
好吗？

1912
01:29:38.950 --> 01:29:39.210
Okay.
好的。

1913
01:29:39.410 --> 01:29:44.530
I can be holding a little jar of sourdough starter, and you can be holding something, too.
我可以拿着一小罐酸种酵母，你也可以拿点什么。

1914
01:29:44.530 --> 01:29:45.910
A glass of wine.
一杯红酒。

1915
01:29:46.250 --> 01:29:46.490
Sure.
当然可以。

1916
01:29:46.810 --> 01:29:51.270
You open up the refrigerator to us, but you can put your own photo in there.
你打开冰箱就能看到我们，但你也可以把自己的照片放进去。

1917
01:29:51.410 --> 01:29:53.410
Or we can just be on your refrigerator.
或者我们也可以直接待在你的冰箱上。

1918
01:29:53.670 --> 01:29:54.630
We'd be happy to be there.
我们很乐意待在那里。

1919
01:29:54.730 --> 01:29:55.590
To keep you company.
陪着你。

1920
01:29:55.830 --> 01:29:56.290
Sure.
当然。

1921
01:29:56.610 --> 01:29:59.010
Well, you guys, that was Phyllis' wedding.
好了，伙计们，以上就是菲利斯的婚礼内容。

1922
01:29:59.010 --> 01:30:02.930
A huge thank you to Phyllis Smith for sending in those audio files.
非常感谢菲利斯·史密斯寄来这些音频文件。

1923
01:30:03.150 --> 01:30:06.710
And of course, oh my gosh, thank you, Ken Whittingham.
当然，天哪，还要谢谢你，肯·惠廷汉姆。

1924
01:30:07.170 --> 01:30:07.650
Yes.
是的。

1925
01:30:07.890 --> 01:30:09.730
Guys, we love you.
伙计们，我们爱你们。

1926
01:30:09.730 --> 01:30:10.910
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1927
01:30:11.050 --> 01:30:11.310
Yeah.
好的。

1928
01:30:11.550 --> 01:30:11.870
Bye.
再见。

1929
